  "claim": "A drummer became the only Australian-born member of the band, when the individual who played bass guitar on rock band Cheetah third LP, left the band. That LP was released in Australia and in Europe in 1976. The drummer was in the Australian band Buster Brown.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Mark Evans (musician). Sentence: Mark Whitmore Evans (born 2 March 1956) is an Australian bass guitarist for the Australian rock band Rose Tattoo who was an early member of hard rock band AC/DC from March 1975 to June 1977.\nPage: Mark Evans (musician). Sentence: His playing featured on their albums \"T.N.T\", \"High Voltage\", \"Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap\", \"Let There Be Rock\" and \"'74 Jailbreak\".\nPage: Mark Evans (musician). Sentence: Evans' autobiography, \"Dirty Deeds: My Life Inside/Outside of AC/DC\" was released in December 2011.\nPage: Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap. Sentence: Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap is an album by Australian hard rock band AC/DC.\nPage: Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap. Sentence: It was the band's third LP released in Australia and in Europe in 1976 but was not released in the US until 1981, more than one year after Bon Scott's death.\nPage: Phil Rudd. Sentence: Upon the 1977 departure of bass guitarist Mark Evans from AC/DC, Rudd became the only Australian-born member of the band.\nPage: Buster Brown (Australian band). Sentence: Buster Brown was an Australian rock and roll band, which featured vocalist Angry Anderson and drummer Phil Rudd, that was formed in Melbourne in 1973.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Mark Evans (musician). Sentence: Mark Whitmore Evans (born 2 March 1956) is an Australian bass guitarist for the Australian rock band Rose Tattoo who was an early member of hard rock band AC/DC from March 1975 to June 1977.\nPage: Mark Evans (musician). Sentence: His playing featured on their albums \"T.N.T\", \"High Voltage\", \"Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap\", \"Let There Be Rock\" and \"'74 Jailbreak\".\nPage: Mark Evans (musician). Sentence: Evans' autobiography, \"Dirty Deeds: My Life Inside/Outside of AC/DC\" was released in December 2011.\nPage: Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap. Sentence: Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap is an album by Australian hard rock band AC/DC.\nPage: Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap. Sentence: It was the band's third LP released in Australia and in Europe in 1976 but was not released in the US until 1981, more than one year after Bon Scott's death.\nPage: Phil Rudd. Sentence: Upon the 1977 departure of bass guitarist Mark Evans from AC/DC, Rudd became the only Australian-born member of the band.\nPage: Buster Brown (Australian band). Sentence: Buster Brown was an Australian rock and roll band, which featured vocalist Angry Anderson and drummer Phil Rudd, that was formed in Melbourne in 1973.",
